            <ArticleTitle>Quebrachitol: Global Status and Basic Research.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-122</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s13659-017-0120-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recently, there has been a renewed interest in the natural-products-inspired drugs. Quebrachitol (QCT) is one of naturally occurring optically active cyclitols that has now received considerable attention. Until the last decade, it came to be a starting point for the lead discovery. In this review, we had a discussion on the basic research of QCT, including its source, structure, properties, and the recent advances on its application. The biological activities and QCT-inspired leads that are potentially effective for treating human diseases were also discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
